research/audit/wave9-dispatch/audit-refuter-a6r2-ex-bounded-with-no-local-extremum-and-nowhere-semicontinuous.prompt.md-1661-[L1] **Assume the Axiom of Choice.** Then a Hamel basis $B$ exists; for $b_{\star} \in B$ the coefficient map $\Lambda_{b_{\star}} : \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{Q}$ is well defined, additive, $\mathbb{Q}$-homogeneous, has range all of $\mathbb{Q}$, has $\{x : \Lambda_{b_{\star}}(x) = 0\} = W$, and $W \ne \{0\}$ ([[lem-hamel-basis-exists]], claims 1, 4 and 5, [[def-linear-combination-and-span]], [[def-linear-subspace]]).
